<title>FRANCE: EU grants free-mkt wheat, barley, rye, rejects oats.</title>
<headline>EU grants free-mkt wheat, barley, rye, rejects oats.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following rebates to export free-market grain to non-EU countries, member-country officials said.</p>
<p>			 Tonnage		Maximum rebate</p>
<p> Soft wheat	  397,500		11.94 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Barley		237,500		28.99 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Durum wheat	  13,300		 5.98 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Rye		    11,000		31.99 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Oats		   Rejected</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
